1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,628
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,712 --> 00:00:06,589
‪["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,719
- ♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪
- ♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,887
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,971 --> 00:00:16,725
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:18,768
[Atoy] <i>Where are the children?</i>
<i>Give me back the children!</i>

7
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:22,230
I'll make these kids suffer.
I'll profit from them.

8
00:00:22,313 --> 00:00:23,940
[Velma] That's Red's child, right?

9
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:26,067
Or maybe you're your father's spy?

10
00:00:26,151 --> 00:00:27,819
Why did my parents turn out like that?

11
00:00:27,902 --> 00:00:29,571
Good thing you didn't take
after your parents.

12
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:32,449
[Atoy] <i>We need to know where they</i>
<i>could have taken the children.</i>

13
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:34,159
<i>V. Starts with a V.</i>

14
00:00:34,242 --> 00:00:35,410
Ve-- Velora Bay!

15
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:37,662
It's in the classified data!
I need the laptop.

16
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:39,831
[Atoy] That's a huge place. Where is that?

17
00:00:39,914 --> 00:00:41,833
[Lily, in English] It's posing
as a high-end beach resort,

18
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:45,128
but it's actually one
of the big concentration camps of…

19
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:46,504
the terrorist group Obsidian.

20
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:49,382
[in English] That's the international
human trafficking syndicate.

21
00:00:49,466 --> 00:00:51,217
[in English] Yes. One and only.

22
00:00:51,301 --> 00:00:52,761
Who owns that island?

23
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:57,640
[Mercado] <i>That is Mr. Edison Kalaf,</i>
<i>the owner of Velora Bay.</i>

24
00:00:57,724 --> 00:01:00,852
<i>He has a club here that he often visits</i>

25
00:01:00,935 --> 00:01:02,812
<i>at this time of the year.</i>

26
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:05,065
[Atoy] <i>Where is this club?</i>
<i>I want to go there.</i>

27
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:07,525
[Trinity, in English]
This is a special event.

28
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:12,947
Okay, where groups will battle
in drag performances.

29
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:17,494
[in English] The winners will be invited
to perform

30
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:23,458
at Mr. Edison Kalaf's 60th birthday bash.

31
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:25,084
[Atoy] <i>Do you know how to dance?</i>

32
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:26,377
[Paldo] Dance? Like this?

33
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:27,754
Why, 'Toy? What are you planning?

34
00:01:27,837 --> 00:01:30,465
[Atoy] We'll perform.
But we need to go all out.

35
00:01:30,548 --> 00:01:32,217
Really all out so we'll win.

36
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:35,011
Fabulous!

37
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:37,555
Will they torture us? Kill us? Like that?

38
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:39,557
Don't think about that.

39
00:01:39,641 --> 00:01:43,520
[Atoy] <i>Attach this to Trinity's collar,</i>
<i>Kalaf's assistant.</i>

40
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:45,188
- [Emerson] <i>What is this?</i>
- [Atoy] <i>Listening device.</i>

41
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:48,608
[Trinity] <i>The usual, the shipment</i>
<i>will be in transit from Velora Bay.</i>

42
00:01:48,691 --> 00:01:51,444
Which are women and young children.

43
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:54,572
You're really bratty even here, huh?
You need your tongue cut off.

44
00:01:54,656 --> 00:01:55,782
- [grunts]
- [Ibyang sobs]

45
00:01:55,865 --> 00:01:59,285
I'm your niece! We're family!

46
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:00,954
Family isn't about being related by blood.

47
00:02:01,037 --> 00:02:04,249
Your mother infuriates me.
Especially when I see you!

48
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:06,251
‪PREVIOUSLY

49
00:02:06,334 --> 00:02:08,419
[music swells]

50
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:11,297
[music fades]

51
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:14,843
Is it done?

52
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:18,429
It's done. You seem in a hurry.

53
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:21,349
I just want to go to church.
They're already there.

54
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:33,903
You know, Karla, I just noticed.

55
00:02:35,196 --> 00:02:38,992
Why do you and Gavin seem allergic
to each other? Aren't you friends?

56
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:43,955
He's just avoiding me
because he thinks… we're already together.

57
00:02:44,455 --> 00:02:48,293
- [sneaky music playing]
- Hey. I didn't know that, ah.

58
00:02:48,793 --> 00:02:52,005
You're fast, faster than me even.

59
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:54,966
Come here, give me a kiss.

60
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:57,010
Hey! Stop that!

61
00:02:57,093 --> 00:02:59,971
- [chuckles]
- Do you want me to cut your lips?

62
00:03:01,472 --> 00:03:02,891
- Come on.
- [music continues]

63
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:05,560
I thought we were together?

64
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:08,855
[in English] So, okay. Let me guess.

65
00:03:11,357 --> 00:03:12,609
[sneaky music playing]

66
00:03:12,692 --> 00:03:16,696
You probably told Gavin
we're together because…

67
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:21,326
you know he likes you.

68
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:25,538
But he has a girlfriend.
Of course, you're hurt now.

69
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:29,208
You don't want to show him you're hurt…

70
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,086
so you said we're together.

71
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:34,505
Mm-hmm.

72
00:03:35,131 --> 00:03:37,550
I don't know what you're talking about.
You talk too much.

73
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:39,594
[music continues]

74
00:03:39,677 --> 00:03:40,762
You know…

75
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:43,223
just choose me instead.

76
00:03:43,806 --> 00:03:45,183
Hey! No way!

77
00:03:45,266 --> 00:03:46,935
[music fades]

78
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:50,063
So, you're semi-rejecting me now, huh?

79
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:53,274
But fine. That's okay.

80
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:56,736
It's okay with me.
I'll go along with it, maybe…

81
00:03:56,819 --> 00:03:58,238
you know?

82
00:03:58,321 --> 00:03:59,948
You'll develop feelings for me.

83
00:04:01,574 --> 00:04:03,576
- [scoffs] Dream on, Uno.
- Ouch.

84
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:07,747
You two are so ambiguous, huh?

85
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:10,041
You're both petty, huh?

86
00:04:11,376 --> 00:04:13,628
- [upbeat music]
- The children are missing,

87
00:04:13,711 --> 00:04:16,506
and you still can't be honest
with yourselves.

88
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:18,383
[scoffs] So petty.

89
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:21,886
[upbeat music playing]

90
00:04:23,179 --> 00:04:24,013
Right?

91
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:50,832
[music fades]

92
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:53,167
- [sewing machine whirring]
- [theme music starts]

93
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:55,420
[theme music playing]

94
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:57,338
[motorcycle revving]

95
00:04:57,422 --> 00:04:58,298
[sewing machine whirring]

96
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,259
- [scratches]
- [snipping]

97
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:05,138
[sewing machine clacking]

98
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:06,848
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

99
00:05:06,931 --> 00:05:08,516
- [thumps & gunshots]
- [music intensifies]

100
00:05:08,599 --> 00:05:10,810
[clicking]

101
00:05:10,893 --> 00:05:12,895
[snipping]

102
00:05:14,022 --> 00:05:18,234
- [music swells]
- [electronic blipping]

103
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,446
[music fades]

104
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:24,240
[muffled chatter in the distance]

105
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:28,703
[sensual funky music playing]

106
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:48,014
[music continues]

107
00:06:03,446 --> 00:06:05,239
- [music fades]
- Hello, ladies!

108
00:06:05,323 --> 00:06:06,908
What's your group's name?

109
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:07,950
Us?

110
00:06:08,034 --> 00:06:09,077
[in English] Oh, we are the…

111
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:12,914
[all] Karayom Kweens!

112
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:15,792
Oww!

113
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:17,168
So, it's you.

114
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:18,294
Uh-huh, mm-hmm.

115
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:21,839
[in English] I'm the leader,
slash, choreographer

116
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:23,174
of The Glitter…

117
00:06:23,257 --> 00:06:25,009
- Bombz!
- Oh!

118
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:29,722
The three-peat champion
of the Reyna Royale Rumble.

119
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:32,266
[in English] And you are?

120
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:33,601
- Me?
- Mmm.

121
00:06:33,684 --> 00:06:35,686
I'm Antonia.

122
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:38,898
[in English] Leader, slash,
costume designer.

123
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:40,399
And your name is?

124
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:45,404
[sneaky music playing]

125
00:06:46,322 --> 00:06:47,615
Chiquita?

126
00:06:47,698 --> 00:06:50,910
[music continues]

127
00:06:51,494 --> 00:06:52,453
Velma!

128
00:06:53,621 --> 00:06:55,081
You know each other?

129
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:56,874
[muffled chatter in distance]

130
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,793
Very well!

131
00:06:59,877 --> 00:07:02,338
She used to be my and Bunda's BFF!

132
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:04,799
But because she stole my makeup kit

133
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:08,928
and I couldn't perform,
we've been FO forever!

134
00:07:09,011 --> 00:07:10,596
[others] Oh!

135
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:16,310
Well, I only did that
because you stole my boyfriend.

136
00:07:16,894 --> 00:07:18,020
You're a snake!

137
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:19,105
[others gasp]

138
00:07:19,188 --> 00:07:20,773
Ay, you're crazy.

139
00:07:20,857 --> 00:07:24,277
I didn't steal anything from you,
because I'm prettier than you!

140
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:26,320
[jeering]

141
00:07:26,404 --> 00:07:28,573
And it really came from you, huh.

142
00:07:29,907 --> 00:07:33,077
Wait. What are you doing here?
"No pets allowed" here, right?

143
00:07:33,161 --> 00:07:34,787
- Oh.
- [Chiquita] And…

144
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:36,581
maybe you're just stalking me.

145
00:07:36,664 --> 00:07:38,958
And why would I do that, huh?

146
00:07:39,041 --> 00:07:40,585
Are you special?

147
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:42,003
[laughs]

148
00:07:42,086 --> 00:07:45,715
[Nestor] Oh, uh-- Uh, Chi… Chiquita, uh,
Velma is our choreographer.

149
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:47,008
She's not our pet.

150
00:07:47,091 --> 00:07:49,010
[others] Ohh!

151
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:50,928
- Really?
- Mm-hmm.

152
00:07:51,012 --> 00:07:53,639
Well, you won't win.

153
00:07:54,223 --> 00:07:58,603
Amateurs like you
will never take our crown.

154
00:07:58,686 --> 00:08:00,062
Says who?

155
00:08:00,146 --> 00:08:03,316
And mark that on your ugly foreheads!

156
00:08:03,399 --> 00:08:04,901
- [others] Oh!
- [Chiquita] Come on, girls!

157
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:05,902
It's suffocating here.

158
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:10,156
- [Atoy] Ay, ay!
- [playful music playing]

159
00:08:10,239 --> 00:08:11,949
- [Nestor] It stinks here!
- [Atoy] Ay, ay.

160
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:14,660
Crazy. It's really dusty, huh?

161
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:15,995
[gasps]

162
00:08:16,078 --> 00:08:17,246
[Nestor] You're crazy!

163
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:20,333
That's crazy, huh. Not even good yet.

164
00:08:20,416 --> 00:08:22,752
That's them.

165
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:25,963
That's the Glitter Bombz.

166
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:30,593
I saw their dance performances, they
are really amazing. They own the killer…

167
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:31,677
death drop!

168
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:34,305
They're really trained in dance,
they're very good.

169
00:08:35,306 --> 00:08:37,433
Atoy, we'll lose to them.

170
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:40,478
Exactly, I watched them.
They're really good, eh.

171
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:43,397
How do we beat them, right?

172
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:46,234
No matter what, we need to beat them.

173
00:08:46,817 --> 00:08:47,652
Correct.

174
00:08:48,486 --> 00:08:49,529
We can do it!

175
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:50,613
[Nestor] Huh?

176
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:53,199
Don't worry. I got you.

177
00:08:53,282 --> 00:08:54,951
[playful music playing]

178
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:56,536
Because we are the…

179
00:08:57,161 --> 00:09:01,582
[all] Karayom Kweens!

180
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:04,585
[music fades]

181
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:13,636
♪ <i>Don't rush the feelings</i> ♪

182
00:09:14,136 --> 00:09:18,641
♪ <i>Of my heart</i> ♪

183
00:09:18,724 --> 00:09:24,689
♪ <i>That's no stranger to this</i> ♪

184
00:09:24,772 --> 00:09:30,069
- ♪ <i>And always at stake…</i> ♪
- ♪ <i>And always at stake…</i> ♪

185
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:32,071
Oh! Here it is, guys!

186
00:09:32,154 --> 00:09:35,449
[in English] Your food and drinks!
Courtesy of Brother Kurt!

187
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:36,993
Thank you, Brother Kurt!

188
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:38,452
[in English] Thank you, Kurt.

189
00:09:38,536 --> 00:09:42,790
[in English] Oh! Gavin. I watched
Cathy's latest vlog, it was ah…

190
00:09:42,873 --> 00:09:46,669
something like breaking up
or getting over heartbreak and uh…

191
00:09:46,752 --> 00:09:50,047
Was that about you? Or… Did you break up?

192
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:53,926
[in English] Yes. A few days ago.

193
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:57,471
Ah, why didn't you tell me?

194
00:09:57,555 --> 00:09:59,223
Why do I need to tell you?

195
00:09:59,307 --> 00:10:01,726
Why care about our relationship?
Don't you have a boyfriend?

196
00:10:01,809 --> 00:10:04,770
Oh! Karla, you have a boyfriend? Who?

197
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:07,898
Why didn't you tell me, Gavin?

198
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:10,151
Didn't I act as a bridge
between you and Cathy?

199
00:10:10,234 --> 00:10:12,403
And now I find out
from someone else that you broke up?

200
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:15,865
What? Surprise?

201
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:16,991
[Gavin] What's your problem?

202
00:10:17,074 --> 00:10:19,577
Well, you surprised us
when you and Uno got together.

203
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:21,704
You didn't even tell me you liked him.

204
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:25,166
Oh, Gavin, it's like…
Why are you angry at Karla?

205
00:10:25,249 --> 00:10:26,125
No.

206
00:10:26,208 --> 00:10:28,461
[in English] Look. I'm okay,
and I'm happy for her.

207
00:10:29,503 --> 00:10:30,463
I'm moving on from Cathy.

208
00:10:30,546 --> 00:10:32,089
Actually, I'm already dating someone, eh.

209
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:34,050
[Gavin] I'll just go out, ah.

210
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:37,136
[music continues]

211
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:43,351
[in English] Karla, I, ah…
I thought you liked Gavin, so…

212
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:44,644
Why Uno?

213
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:48,314
Eh, please, Brother Kurt. Don't meddle.

214
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:53,194
Sorry, huh. I'm not meddling.

215
00:10:56,113 --> 00:11:01,619
["Sa Wala" by Wickermoss
with Neth Macam playing]

216
00:11:05,539 --> 00:11:09,919
Aww. Babe, I miss you too.

217
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:13,714
[footsteps tapping]

218
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:16,092
- You can join.
- [clears throat] Chiquita,

219
00:11:16,175 --> 00:11:18,094
let's talk.

220
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:21,180
[in English] Talk to the hand.

221
00:11:21,263 --> 00:11:22,515
You annoy me!

222
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:27,353
Uhm, Chiquita, uh, let me be honest.

223
00:11:27,436 --> 00:11:33,025
You know, there are more important things,
bigger things than your fight with Velma.

224
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:36,195
Be direct with me. What do you need?

225
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:38,406
Um…

226
00:11:39,448 --> 00:11:41,659
there are missing children,

227
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:44,412
and we suspect
they were taken to Velora Bay.

228
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:48,124
Where your boss' birthday will be held.

229
00:11:48,207 --> 00:11:51,585
That's why we need
to win this contest, to get there.

230
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:53,295
This is the only way we found.

231
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:55,089
So, what is this?

232
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:56,674
[in English] Game fixing?

233
00:11:56,757 --> 00:11:59,176
We'll perform badly just for you?

234
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:02,304
[clears throat] Chiquita, listen. Okay?

235
00:12:02,388 --> 00:12:05,141
We know your group
is more experienced than ours,

236
00:12:05,224 --> 00:12:07,601
and we don't intend to take your crown.

237
00:12:07,685 --> 00:12:10,813
But, please.
Children's lives are at stake here!

238
00:12:10,896 --> 00:12:12,731
[Emerson] Yes. And also…

239
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:15,276
we're not after the prize.

240
00:12:15,359 --> 00:12:18,404
We can give you the prize in full.
If that's-- if that's what you want.

241
00:12:18,988 --> 00:12:21,073
And besides, girl, you know me.

242
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:24,201
You know I wouldn't talk to you
if it wasn't important, right?

243
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:26,287
So please, cooperate.

244
00:12:26,954 --> 00:12:28,372
Mmm? Do you want proof?

245
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:29,790
- All right.
- Oh.

246
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:32,168
[Velma] Here are the pictures
of the missing children, oh.

247
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:33,377
They're cute, right?

248
00:12:33,461 --> 00:12:36,297
Oh. They're really cute, huh?

249
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:38,090
One even looks like my niece.

250
00:12:38,174 --> 00:12:39,341
Mmm, right?

251
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:42,470
All we want is to return them
to their parents.

252
00:12:43,679 --> 00:12:44,763
Aww.

253
00:12:45,723 --> 00:12:47,016
In fairness…

254
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:50,144
- You tell stories well, huh?
- [tense music]

255
00:12:50,227 --> 00:12:54,231
[Chiquita] You even have these stories
about kidnappings of children.

256
00:12:54,815 --> 00:12:56,358
I don't believe you.

257
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:59,069
No. What I'm saying is true.

258
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:00,279
Oh, no.

259
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:04,658
I won't be swayed
by your pity effect, huh.

260
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:07,828
And you have the nerve to approach me.

261
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:10,789
Here's the deal. Let's put it this way.

262
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:13,959
May the best drag group win.

263
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:17,963
Unfortunately, that's not you.

264
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:19,089
Step aside.

265
00:13:19,715 --> 00:13:22,718
[tense music playing]

266
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:27,556
We can't do anything.

267
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,016
[in English] No choice…

268
00:13:29,099 --> 00:13:31,060
It seems we really have no choice but…

269
00:13:32,686 --> 00:13:36,899
superbly slay this contest.

270
00:13:37,942 --> 00:13:39,318
- [music fades]
- That's it.

271
00:13:41,987 --> 00:13:43,405
[upbeat music]

272
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:45,115
Hey.

273
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:50,955
[upbeat music continues]

274
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:03,968
[upbeat dance music]

275
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:16,855
[music ends]

276
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:19,567
[in English] Hello, hello!

277
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:24,780
Hello, queens, divas, gays,

278
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:27,616
and all allies!

279
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:30,327
[in English] Welcome, welcome, welcome!

280
00:14:30,411 --> 00:14:36,417
Tonight, the spotlight
is hotter than your ex's DMs.

281
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,711
- [audience] Ohh! Yes!
- Because…

282
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:42,882
this is the fiercest, loudest,

283
00:14:42,965 --> 00:14:47,678
and the most fabulous
drag showdown of the year,

284
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:50,014
the Reyna Royale Rumble!

285
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:53,517
[audience cheering]

286
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:58,522
Before anything else, I would like
to thank each and every one of you

287
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:02,026
- for making this competition possible.
- [upbeat music]

288
00:15:02,109 --> 00:15:03,277
[audience applauding]

289
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:07,865
So, before I judge the competition,

290
00:15:08,449 --> 00:15:11,994
I would like to hand this mic
to our host for tonight.

291
00:15:12,077 --> 00:15:13,996
Please welcome, Tiny!

292
00:15:14,079 --> 00:15:17,750
- [audience cheering]
- [music continues]

293
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:19,084
Hi! Mmm.

294
00:15:19,168 --> 00:15:21,754
[smooches] Oh, do your best. Okay?

295
00:15:21,837 --> 00:15:24,632
Thank you very much, Boss Trina!

296
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:27,593
Let's give her
a round of applause, everyone!

297
00:15:27,676 --> 00:15:30,012
- [audience cheering]
- And of course,

298
00:15:30,095 --> 00:15:31,722
let's not delay any longer!

299
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:35,726
I know everyone is ready!

300
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:40,105
Is it okay to hear your applause
with screams?

301
00:15:40,189 --> 00:15:42,858
[audience cheering]

302
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:47,321
Whoops! Here it is!
Let's welcome to the stage…

303
00:15:47,404 --> 00:15:49,657
the Glitter Bombz!

304
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:51,533
- [audience cheering]
- [upbeat music playing]

305
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:54,119
Reigning champ, reigning champ.

306
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:57,206
- [audience applauding]
- [music continues]

307
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:06,006
[audience applauding]

308
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:11,387
[music continues]

309
00:16:16,684 --> 00:16:19,436
[audience cheering]

310
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:30,990
They're good.

311
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:38,080
[music continues]

312
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:07,818
[Tiny, in English] Thank you so much,
Glitter Bombz!

313
00:17:07,901 --> 00:17:12,698
Make some noise for Glitter Bombz!

314
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:16,952
Here it is! The act
that will tear down the stage!

315
00:17:17,036 --> 00:17:19,038
The powerhouse performance!

316
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:21,123
Let's give it up for

317
00:17:21,206 --> 00:17:23,625
- Velvet and Vixens!
- [audience applauding]

318
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:27,463
- [cool upbeat music playing]
- [audience whooping]

319
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:32,885
[music continues]

320
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:41,185
[audience cheering]

321
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:06,710
[audience cheering]

322
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:10,506
[Tiny, in English] Thank you so much,
Velvet and Vixens!

323
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:12,382
Ah, they're newcomers.

324
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:15,385
But they really showed
something different.

325
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:19,181
[in English] Congratulations in advance,
Velvet and Vixens!

326
00:18:19,264 --> 00:18:21,058
Now, could this next one…

327
00:18:21,141 --> 00:18:24,436
really pass through the eye of the needle?

328
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,647
- [audience cheering]
- Could this be

329
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:30,859
the international performance level?

330
00:18:31,443 --> 00:18:34,196
Come on! Let's welcome to the stage…

331
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:39,284
The Karayom Kweens!

332
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:43,413
- [audience cheering]
- [upbeat music playing]

333
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:46,792
[audience cheering]

334
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:48,585
[music continues]

335
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:51,213
[audience cheering]

336
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:55,217
[audience cheering]

337
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:57,511
[audience whooping]

338
00:19:04,893 --> 00:19:06,854
[music continues]

339
00:19:12,734 --> 00:19:14,820
[audience clapping]

340
00:19:14,903 --> 00:19:16,238
[audience whoops]

341
00:19:17,823 --> 00:19:19,825
- [audience whoops]
- [music continues]

342
00:19:19,908 --> 00:19:21,827
[laughing]

343
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:39,970
- [music continues]
- [audience cheering]

344
00:19:57,321 --> 00:19:59,448
[music continues]

345
00:20:10,209 --> 00:20:12,085
[music fades]

346
00:20:12,169 --> 00:20:14,630
[audience applauding]

347
00:20:14,713 --> 00:20:18,592
[Tiny] Once again, the Karayom Kweens!

348
00:20:18,675 --> 00:20:19,885
[in English] Very good!

349
00:20:19,968 --> 00:20:22,095
[upbeat music]

350
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:26,642
Looks like we'll have a tough time.

351
00:20:26,725 --> 00:20:28,727
[music continues]

352
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:34,191
[in English] So, are you guys excited?

353
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:36,610
[audience cheering] Yes!

354
00:20:36,693 --> 00:20:39,112
Excited, Glitter Bombz?

355
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:41,531
- [exclaims]
- Excited, Karayom Kweens?

356
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:43,825
Here are our top two contenders.

357
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:46,995
They got the highest scores,

358
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:50,082
and they will battle
for the Reyna Royale crown!

359
00:20:50,916 --> 00:20:53,001
[in English] We have, of course…

360
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:55,629
The Glitter Bombz!

361
00:20:55,712 --> 00:20:57,923
[audience cheering]

362
00:20:58,006 --> 00:21:02,302
And the challengers, the newcomers…

363
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:04,513
the Karayom Kweens!

364
00:21:04,596 --> 00:21:06,306
[audience cheering]

365
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:12,312
[Trinity] And this is the moment
we've all been waiting for.

366
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:14,398
[audience cheering]

367
00:21:14,481 --> 00:21:16,775
Okay? Here it is.

368
00:21:16,858 --> 00:21:21,321
[in English]
With a jaw-breaking score of 92.7…

369
00:21:21,405 --> 00:21:22,906
[audience cheering]

370
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:25,617
Oh, my god! I'm so nervous!

371
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:28,704
- [audience cheering]
- [Trinity laughing]

372
00:21:29,413 --> 00:21:31,498
- [music swells]
- [Atoy] <i>Give this to us, Lord.</i>

373
00:21:31,581 --> 00:21:33,583
<i>I just want my children back.</i>

374
00:21:34,209 --> 00:21:36,837
<i>I just want a chance</i>
<i>to rebuild our family.</i>

375
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:38,588
[music fades]

376
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:44,386
- [electronic blipping]
- [intense music playing]

377
00:21:48,890 --> 00:21:50,767
[music fades]

378
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:52,311
- [dramatic music]
<i>- Watch him.</i>

379
00:21:52,394 --> 00:21:54,396
[in English] He might try to infiltrate
Velora Bay.

380
00:21:54,479 --> 00:21:56,106
[in English] Don't worry, sir.

381
00:21:56,773 --> 00:22:00,319
No undesirables have entered
Boss K's island yet.

382
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:03,322
[Trinity] <i>If he shows up,</i>
<i>he will be dead on the spot.</i>

383
00:22:03,405 --> 00:22:04,740
[Mercado] Two access points.

384
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:08,327
<i>Via helicopter, via boat. Padua,</i>

385
00:22:08,410 --> 00:22:11,246
their lives are in your hands.

386
00:22:11,830 --> 00:22:15,125
I'll take care of them, sir.
I'll make sure they're ready.

387
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:17,002
Remember, huh. We are the main event

388
00:22:17,085 --> 00:22:20,130
and also the main distraction,
so we need to do our best.

389
00:22:20,213 --> 00:22:21,631
‪UP NEXT

390
00:22:21,715 --> 00:22:25,218
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor, holding the scissors</i> ♪

391
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:28,513
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

392
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:30,057
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

393
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,767
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
